# What NOT to upload when deploying to Cloud Run.
#
# Without this file gcloud falls back to .gitignore and uploads everything else
# — including the 300MB+ .git folder — which made the source upload time out
# and fail the deploy.
#
# The container only needs client/, server.js, config.js and the package files.
# See the Dockerfile: nothing else is ever COPYed in.

# The repository history. Big, and the container has no use for it.
.git/
.gitattributes

# Reinstalled inside the image by `npm ci`.
node_modules/
client/node_modules/

# Rebuilt inside the image by `npm run build`.
/build
/client/build

# Full-size camera originals; the web-sized copies in client/public are used.
/media-originals

# Secrets. Production reads these from GCP Secret Manager, never from a file.
.env
.env.*

# Runtime data mirrored to GCS — the server downloads these at boot.
subscribers.csv
registrations.csv
coaching-bookings.csv

# Editor and OS clutter
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Camera originals that live in client/public but nothing on the site loads —
# the web-sized .mp4 next to each one is what the pages actually use. Together
# they are ~255MB, which is enough to make the source upload time out with a
# 408. They stay on disk and in git; they just don't need to ship.
# (noah-testimonial.mov IS used, on the home page, so it is not listed here.)
/client/public/images/separate showcase example.MOV
/client/public/images/s2-riya-holt-video.MOV
/client/public/images/s2-srihari-final-presentation.MOV
/client/public/images/oscar-testimonial.mov
